/// Balances at the start of the ledger: Jamie's checking account, the day before the closing.
opening 2024-12-18
  checking    128_000 USD

/// Closing day. The loan contract originates 279,000.00 USD into rental-bank;
/// its loan-contract assertions reconcile the principal and payoff. Cash to close
/// is the 25% down payment, 4,850.00 USD of basis costs, 3,120.00 USD of loan
/// costs and 722.30 USD of prepaid interest.
2024-12-18 checking -> rental-bank 108_000 USD #transfer
2024-12-18 home-loan
2024-12-18 rental-bank -> title-co 376_850 USD #purchase of house

/// The loan costs are a cost of the loan for as long as the loan lasts. Written here after the sale, the range
/// ends the day the loan was paid off: paid now, deducted evenly per day over those 377 days.
2024-12-18..2025-12-29 rental-bank -> lender 3_120 USD #loan-cost of house
2024-12-18 rental-bank -> lender 722.30 USD #interest of house
2024-12-31 rental-bank = 6_307.70 USD
2024-12-31 checking = 20_000.00 USD
2024-12-31 home-loan = 279_000 USD
